  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Connecting Communities:Digital Public Service Transformation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UNJP aims at creating the conditions to foster digital transformation in Mozambique through (i) a comprehensive assessment of the country&#x2019;s digital public ecosystem and (ii) the implementation of a pilot to increase connectivity and access to digital services at district level, while immersing local communities in the use of digital services. The project prioritizes gender equality by addressing barriers faced by women and girls, promoting digital literacy, and enhancing their representation in decision-making. It adopts a human rights-based approach, emphasizing equitable access to information and governance processes. Furthermore, the project commits to leaving no one behind, targeting marginalized populations such as persons with disabilities, ethnic minorities, and rural communities. Through these integrated approaches, the project aims to not only advance digitalization but also contribute to inclusive development, gender equality, and upholding human rights in Mozambique.</narrative>
  </description>
